She's cordiary and sparse, and she wins you up close.
Tell us what you're doing in Paris.
I have come to introduce a new collection, which my sister Penélope and I designed for Mango for this autumn-winter season, and at the same time I took part in announcing the second year "Mango Fashion Awards" and Dinner at Oper in honor of Valentino.
So it's been a challenging, but at the same time an exciting day at the same time.
What is your new collection for Mango, for which you have been working for for the fourth season?
Me and my sister love films from the 50's and 60's and we drew a lot of stimuli from them.
I also love wandering around the city and obscuring women how they go dressed, how they combine and line up their clothes very often.
You're a dancewoman, an actor, a very versatile woman, isn't you?
I don’t think so, but after all, it’s all intertwined.
For example, I liked the clothes since I was a child, I still wanted to go to my grandma's, go through my aunt's closets and look at her clothes.
It was a sensation, almost better than going on a pilgrimage.
When I became a dancer, I’ve always tried to take care of the way I’m dressed.
However, you know that we dancers pride ourselves on how we're groomed to feel good in our lessons and rehearsals while looking in the mirror.
And as an actress, when they give you a costume, that's when you're going to really get into a character.
So everything is intertwined, of course, with great respect for designers and professionalism.
You've been 30 recently, did the crisis fall on you?
Oh, no.
I'm feeling better than I've ever used to, I've enjoyed my thirties.
I find out that a woman is already done, she has experience and she enjoys life with fewer mistakes.
Biological clock doesn't scare me.
Since childhood I do what I want, and this gives me great inner happiness.
So you're thinking about being a mother, don't you?
Of course I'm going to be a mussement, because my body asks, and besides, I want to be a young mum, I don't want to miss it.
When it comes to my father, I don’t worry about that.
But one thing I know for sure, I'm going to give my child a sense of happiness and I'm going to nuril him with a lot of love.
When it comes to the movie, you've got a few premieres of the movies you made last year.
That's right and I'm looking forward to coming to cinemas.
I'm coming from theatricaal world, so I'm very impatient and restless, I just want everything right now and of course I can't.
I'm looking forward to the premiere of "La Tulma Mountain" and "En busca de la tumba de Cristo".
Let's see how you're going to like...
A few days ago you had your premiership at Naomi Campbell's catwalk alongside Naomi Campbell, isn't it?
Well, don't say that.
Isn't like I'm going to stand on a catwalk like a model.
Only Naomi Campbell, whom I've known for for a long time, and she invited me to London to take part in a benefit parade for her "women for a better life" organization, and the clothes we were performing - I also chose two models from our Mango collection - it was auctioned and the proceeds were handed over to Naomin's NGO.
People don't know Naomi has such a good heart.
