Besides, I'm going to stick to the good in which he's engaged.
She's asked me to perform for charitancies, but when he asks me to make a handstand, I'm going to do it, too.
I'm going to do what I'm going to be in favor of third-hundred-world women.
Drivers repeatedly caught with alcohol in their blood will need to install "alcolock"
The Ministry of the Interior asks that the driver with three administrative sanctions for driving under the influence of alcohol has to install a system in his car that prevents him from kick-starting the car drunk or if he does not breathe.
The proposal became known already in June this year and is now included in the annual report of the Prosecutor General's Attorney's Office, according to which it is a pilot project that will last one year.
Its aim is to return the driver behind the wheel, so drivers will also have to undergo a course of traffic re-education.
In addition to the National Traffic Safety Authority, the Directorate-General for Transport (DGT) and the Foundation of the Technology Institute for Automobile Safety (FITSA) will also participate in this experience.
According to statistics, between 30 and 75 per cent of motorists accused more than once for drunk driving will get behind the wheel again in this state.
Alcolock should prevent this as it is a system connected to a vehicle that measures the level of liquor in exhausted air and prevents the vehicle from starting if the driver does not breathe before or if a maximum alcohol concentration is recorded.
Its price exceeds 1 000 euros and the ecclesiaspower himself would have to be reimbursed.
A study carried out at this point in the USA in 2007 showed that vehicles equipped with this equipment decreased by 65% during the first year since the introduction.
In Spain it is expected that 115 people could save their lives every year.
The measure confines administrative sanctions for two reasons: in order to deal with such behaviour before it results in a criminal offense.
And in order to facilitate its introduction, since the legislation can be carried out in the usual way, however, the necessary regulation of criminal provisions requires a change in the law.
The equipment is not yet available on the Spanish market in any sales version, although it has already been re-installed in some industrial cars and public service vehicles.
Just tomorrow, the Congress of Deputies will vote on the PSOE (Spanish Workers' Socialist Party) proposal, in which it is advisable to install this system on school buses, as is the case in France.
