“There’s one boundary line on which there hasn’t been a covenant for a long time, and if there is a good opportunity, in the name of the government, I’m going to take this position again.”
“It is also necessary to revisit our vision of the North in the context of climate change,” he said, talking about the north-stregnation, which will unleash the thaw all-season as a result of thumping glaciers.
In this new geo-political contemplative context, the prime minister thinks it is becoming an tribute.
And what about the inhabitants of the territory, indigenous peoples and Inuites?
The premier has stated that the Quebec government will be very attentive to them and that the project would be beneficial to them, especially to the young.
For-two former mini-season ministers, Pierre Corbeil and Michel Létourneau (former pequis MP from Ungava), have already begun negotiations with about thirty communities.
The activity was launched by the Inter-Ministerial Committee chaired by Benoît Pelletier, in which Julia Boulet (Transport and Natural Resources) takes an important position.
The premier does not preclude a large meeting, "not necessarily a summit", but the moment when "a common vision will be set out."
After all, the development of the North should take place in accordance with the principles of sustainable development.
The North plan will "jointly designed, structured and environmentally friendly," he promised.
Jean Charest described this "vision" fluctually related to the vision of liberal prime ministers who preceded it.
"Even as the liberals who preceded us, we have changed our mindset to turn the challenges into new opportunities for growth and development."
After all, it was one of the ever-tempered themes of the weekend, which on Friday was started with a big cocktail highlighting the 50th anniversary of Jean Lesage’s head of the party.
One of the adopted resolutions proposes to re-Christew the Beauharnois headquarters on Adélard-Godbout's dam.
"From Godbout, who founded Hydro-Québec, through Lesage, who conducted a Calm revolution and the nationalization of hydroelectric power, to Bourass, who created the bay of James, our party was able to shatter the future," Jean Charest said.
Speaking at a press conference, he relied on John Diefenbaker's "Roads to the North" program of John Diefenbaker from 1957 to 1963.
Receipt when it came to Eastmain1a-Ruper dam hydro-electra, Charest stressed that its launch is planned for 2012.
"I only say this between us, but I'm planning to be there," he confided to his membership, sparking considerable applausion.
The same prime minister, who in April said there would be no elections in 2008, and undoubtedly in 2009, he has not ruled out the opportunity to call an election in the autumn of this year, which is permitted by the law.
Nevertheless, he emphasized that his program is packed, especially the federal council mission in China and Québec-New York summit.
The weekend congress has provided the Liberal chief with a platform for some nationalist resolutions, in particular certain "efforts to amend the constitution", which passed very smoothly: PLQ (Liberal Party Québek) is particularly demanding the recognition of the "specificity of Québek" in the Constitution.
Québec also fends to appoint a part of the members of the Canadian Radio and Television Broadcasting Council who would have velocity in the event of decisions taken in Quebec.
From the party of the Opposition, the Plan of the North was skeptically adopted in its main features.
PQ (Parti Québecois) leader Pauline Marois re-exclaimed North Québek's Development Policy, which Landry's government triggered in 2001.
According to her, when the government of the Liberals came to power in 2003, it disembarks the fulfillment of this policy.
If she clung to her, "we'd be on today," Marois remarked alongside her Jean-Talon nominee (whether the elections are taking place today) by Françoise Mercure.
ADQ has said it will support the adoption of the North Plan in the government.
"However, we wish it wasn't a mere spectacle," explained Sébastien Proulx, leader representing Mario Dumont, who is returning from the holidays today.
Letters - Dishonored Land
It was Vic Toews, the ex-Minister of "justice" in Harper's Cabinet, who dared to recuperate about Louis Arbour in the summer of last year that she was "shame" for Canada.
In such a disgrace the unceiving struggle for justice and who deserves all our admiration says a lot about the prime minister's ensuing about Stephen Harper himself.
We have a government in front of us, which is the only one of all participating Western countries not transported back to the homeland of its national locked up in Guantánamo concentration camp.
Omar Khadr was a juricial adolescent.
The only government that, even though Canada has signed the Geneva Convention, denounces its word and leaves rot in the indifferent conditions of a children's soldier.
The only one relied on the parodiment of righteousness to judge the guilt of the defendant.
Recall that UNICEF, Amnesty international and, in particular the Association of Canadian Attorneys, are advocating the repatriation of Omar Khadr, so that he can expect a fair trial in Canada.
The same government closes her eyes to torture: it doesn’t really care that this young man is psychologically devastated in the future, unequivocally, after so many years of torment.
Unrecognized, but we are precisely witnessing the creeping erosion of our rights, our freedom and our "democracy", the word that Harper is wielding so much and which sounds so empty from his mouth.
The time has come when there is no more morality: it is possible to torment a Canadian citizen, difficult to treat him, to imprison him according to the arbitrariness of the head of the hitherto minority government (as it will be after October 14.).
Many electors believe that they will find a bailout in a party that proclaims Virtue, the Law and the Order: they do not see that this government renounced what constituted the repugnation and seriousness of our country.
Shame, Mr. Toews, it is in this renunciation, not anywhere else.
Opinions - Barrick Gold Orwellian Disposers
In the September 17 issue, Le Devoir published a letter from Patrick J. Garver, executive vice-president of the Canadian mining company Barrick Gold.
With the Orwellian logic, it confirms that the world's largest gold maker has launched prosecuting the three authors and the impoverishment little publishing house for librsion in order to provoke a "transparent public debate" and demanding six million of them.
If it is true that judiciary are independent and impartially, they do not judge truthfulness, especially in the case of prosecution for libration, but a law.
Unsurprisingly Garver ignores this crucial distinction.
Or is Barrick Gold the best way to have a public debate break anyone who dared to defend the opposite stance for Barrick Gold?
No matter how the trial turns out, the authors and publisher of Noir Canada (Black Canada) will be compelled to spend respectable sums to be prepared to defend themselves and to fight in a very unequivocal baptism with an army of lawyers supported by almost bottomless pockets of a mining company.
After all, tactic in these unequivmented struggles often consists in ruining the defendants in order to promote conciliation, which clogs the mouth of the opposing party and, moreover, terrifies anyone who dared to dedicate this matter.
If Barrick Gold really wanted a public debate, it was supposed to present its view of the whole thing to a public opinion.
Contrary to what’s going on in several countries where Barrick Gold operates, there’s a debate going on under the normal circumstances in exchanging ideas, and not by a baton.
Mining companies, therefore, were not enough than to reopen their books, their documentation and to establish a real debate through newspapers, the media, the publications and the funding of independent scientific teams that could bring light to the whole thing.
But Barrick Gold doesn’t seem to have any confidence in public posing, and he rejects petties and letters in support of the authors of Noir Canada.
Perhaps Garrver could explain, how can he demand a "priipet debate" and at the same time desponeve the opinions of the same public?
It seems that this word in the vice-presidential world denotes timid lawyers, and not all Canadians; that's a rather duped notion.
In a matter of democracy, they also have the right to be spoken by deceptionists.
Barrick Gold doesn’t understand – or doesn’t want to understand – that the public, which supports authors and publishers Noir Canada, is doing so primarily because he rejects the brutal ways of mining society.
The public is deprived of Barrick and to judge the matter, but based on a civilized exchange of arguments, not within the framework of what many people perceive as a prosecutor in which the defendant's mouth is supposed to be blocked (in its prosecution "published debate", Barrick, by the way, has just filed an official call to the authors of Noir Canada in order to formally notify them that they should stop using this term...).
Apart from Garver's surreal Speech, Prosecuting Barrick Gold is a direct attack on the university's freedom of inquiry and the pursuit of the truth that is essential for every democratic society.
Overall, he denies the right to quotarition of credible sources and to a debate on facts and interpretations that represent the very basis of intellectual activity.
If in a country such as Canada, it is impossible to study and to discuss topics that the rich companies of this world don’t dislike themselves without exopting reproposal, who else will be able to do it?
If Barrick Gold really wanted a public and transparent debate, it could have formed it if it had followed the scientific standards used by Noir Canada authors.
He has the right to an answer.
The University environment to which we belong can manage debates and disagreements and resolvultom conflicts since time immemorial.
Barrick Gold's exaggerated suggaging policy clearly shows that despite what it claims, it doesn't have the slightest tempt to have a transparent debate.
For the university world, this is a loss, as well as a public debate in Canada, and it is time for governments to put in place a measure that would limit this type of unsuccessful prosecution.
Wall Street bail-out operation - Democrats and Republicans understand each other
The Bush administration and congressional leaders, both Republicans and Democrats, finally came to an agreement on the biggest bailout economic plan since the thirties-discussion.
A new version of the $700-billion-dollar plan to hamper the financial crisis, which has been wading through Wall Street for months, has yet to be endorsed by both chambers of Congress.
In particular, it presupposes: better control of chosen representatives over its application, new mechanisms to repay the stored public money, new measures for capturing the number of houses confiscated for non-repayment, as well as the right to monitor the amount of wages disbursed for executives bailed companies.
U.S. Chancellor of Treasury Henry Paulson, House Speaker Nancy Pelosi and the Republican representative at the negotiating table, Senator Judd Gregg, announced the good news yesterday a few minutes after midnight, after the end of a two-day negotiating marathon.
“We have made great strenuous and have come to an agreement that will be effective in the markets,” said Henry Paulson.
"Everything has been done in such a way that a real-world economy and ordinary Americans are safe from the crisis currently taking place on Wall Street," the Democrat said.
"That's a crucial point: if we don't, the trauma, the turquoism, the chaos and the disruption of the daily lives of Americans will be enormous," Republican Judd Gregg said.
Over the last few hours, the negotiations have ramped up at the maximum speed out of the fear of the effect that would have another failure on the mood of investors.
A fixed time limit was the opening of the markets this morning.
Both candidates for U.S. president were invited to the negotiations at a later date, and they both commented more on the deal, without forgetting to express their dissatisfaction with the fact that it was necessary to resort to such an extreme solution.
Democrat Senator Barack Obama has added an injunction of some measures, especially the one aimed at allowing owners to maintain their residence, and measures on the salaries of state-saved by state-salties.
“While we ask taxpayers to take special measures because of the irritability of some people, there is nothing to congratulate.
However, these measures are necessary," he tweeted.
His Republican rival John McCain, who has been questioned by another station asking if he was going to vote for the proposed plan, replied: "I'd like to see the details, but I'd hope it is."
"Gearse traits I've read [supplier] that it's something we'll all have to spend and with the help of which it will be possible to move forward.
Choosing inaction is simply unacceptable," he said.
The 700-billion-dollar plan's goal is to rebuite dubious receivables and risky and unsaleable assets of U.S. financial institutions.
The plan comes after 14 months of crisis unleashed by the rupture bubble in the real estate market, which first led to the collapse of high-risk mortgage loans (subprimes), then transferred to other, more widespread forms of loans (PCAAs) and resulted in cash freeze-of-frozen and the disintegration of banks and financial institutions.
A slump in last week's first-agreement's deal is committed by Republican deputies.
From the moment the Democrats have agreed that some "toxic" assets of companies with difficulties the government will only valuable, but will not rebade them, there is a belief that the hopeless situation is abducted.
In an intriguation of congruent views in Congress, a follow-up has been accompanied a measure stipulating that the government will be able to introduce new fees that would help it retrieve its deposit if, as a result of the program, it will have to assume losses for a period of five years.
The new plan envisages a first-in-commnment deposit of $250 billion, to which it will be possible to add an additional $100 billion if the president finds it necessary.
Another $350 billion will be approved by Congress in a new poll.
By exchanging its aid, Washington will receive stakes in rescued companies, which will pay dividends in the event of a profit and that he will be able to re-sell when it is over.
The federal government will have the opportunity to delay the foreclosing procedures of real estate associated with loans covered by the plan, as well as to set limits on the amount of remuneration and compensation paid to senior executives of the affected firms.
The masterminds of the plan would like to subordinate it to a vote in the Chamber of Deputies already today and in the Senate on Wednesday.
Contributed to allegations made, it is not yet certain whether their plan will have the green light.
Yesterday, voices were further up against the project, both in the Republican and in the Democratic camp.
"Clearly it is quite obvious that Washington can't hear you," Republican Scott Garrett, a member of the Chamber of Deputies' financial commission, said in a statement.
"Yeah, we have a serious financial problem.
Yes, there are solutions.
Proprietors, however, is not a solution.”
Democratic representative Brad Sherman, the moderator of a group of congresswomen nicknamed the "skeptics", presents the whole thing in a different way, but comes to the same conclusion.
"The four hundred esteemed professors of economics, among them the three Nobel laureates, have written to us: we ask Congress not to rush too much and to examine carefully which way to go," he said.
At the same time it was reaffirmed in Europe that this crisis is a world crisis.
At the end of an emergency meeting, three Benelux countries announced the partial nationalization of the Fortis banking group for €11.2 billion ($16.3 billion).
Intervention by the governments of Belgium, the Netherlands, the Netherlands and Luxembourg has emerged after the French bank BNP Paribas announced that it is withdrawing from the purchase of its competitor, which is on the brink since it lost 2 billion euro ($2.9 Billion) as a result of a risky realcretion to buy real estate in the United States.
Fortis employs 85 000 people, is one of Europe's twenty largest banks and one of the ten largest insurers.
“We won’t lose this money,” Dutch Finance Minister Wouter Bos said.
"By return, we are gaining the right to sufficiary and influence.
Saviors and households in today's uncertain times can be appreciated."
On the other side of La Manche's canal so far, the British government seems to have started nationalizing another bank affected by the financial crisis.
According to an English press, the government was supposed to take over all existing Bradford and Bringley, of which more than $41 billion ($5.5 billion) were loans to buy real estate.
According to yesterday's announcement, the Spanish bank Santander's bank will be bought by the branches and accounts of British bank's clients.
Bradford and Bringley will be the second bank after Northern Rock, which the British government must nationalize since the beginning of the financial crisis.
Paul Newman (1925-2008) - The Death of a Socially Engaged Icon
His beauties with azure's eyes for a long time represented his trumpe, according to others a weakness.
Did this American academia with an engrossing smile disappear from daffodils?
Yes and no.
Shyness, sensibilities and unceasing talent that possessed him also distanced him from the power category that beget real stars.
But what a long-distance runner he was!
Paul Newman dies on Friday at the age of 83 at the age of 83 at the Connecticut as a result of Lung cancer and remains one of the last icons of fatty years of U.S. kinematography.
Unparalleled than Brando, to whom he was similar and for a long time his rival on the screen, Newman was a more cautious actor, certainly a more fragiler but also an apostle of freedom and the disintegration of dramatic conventions.
Mixed blood often breeds beautiful children.
He was born in Ohio in 1925, his father was a German Jew and his mother originally a Hungarian.
From these European roots, one of the glorious faces of an American dream was born.
Without an exaggerated e-ego, which is the last sign of quality.
Because in it saw this whole country in love with a self-made man, a warrior at the War in the Pacific, wounded in a battle who studied acting in Yale in the early 50's, then visited New York's Actor's Studio and celebrated a triumph in the theater, on television and soon in film.
The same-equital man who fought for civil rights was also a race car racer who placed second at the 24-Hunger Challenging race at Le Mans in 1979, and at the same time a sex symbol, even though he's been an exemplary couple with actress Joanne Woodward since 1958.
With it, the shady places of this hidden, discreet, socially engaged star are also leaving, alleviating the fuss of their own show-business, which will forever remain quizzically mysterious to some extent.
Deciduous man, in the noblest sense of the word.
Paul Newman's departure this weekend inflicted pitfalls on film lovers, while his big role rivals each other on the canvas of memories.
After him, he defiles for more than half a century the ever-changing U.S. seventh art.
In the memo pour re-emergence the charming cowboy of Butch Cassidy and the Sundance Kid (1969), a young man refusing his sensuous wife (Elizabeth Taylor) in Cat on a Hot Roof, an adaptation of Tennessee Williams from 1958.
From the less ancient past (1990) we recall his sensitive Mr. Bridge, disturbed at an advanced age by a marriage that didn't live up to all expectations.
So many other Newman Pauls have gone down in history.
Boxer Rocky Graziano, crunched, abusive, memorable delinquent from Somebody Up There Likes Me (North Hate) by Robert Wis, a role designed for James Dean, taken over after his death that introduced Newman in 1956 into a true acquaintance.
Sympathetic gangster in absolutely great The Sting, an Oscar for best film in 1973.
Fascinated and vengeful billiard gnawing player in Robert Rossen (1961), starring Martin Scorsese as The Color of Money, which will bring him the only Oscar out of seven nominations in 1987.
This face wandering ever, that was him.
And him again.
Various epocs compete with each other in his professional career.
Young people know him mainly thanks to the iconic Slap Shot George Roy Hill (1977) of Reggie Dunlop, a non-traditional ice hockey coach.
Fans reunited with him in 1994 in The Hudsucker Proxy of the Coen brothers.
He closed his career as godfather of the Irish mafia in Road to Perdition Sam Mendes in 2003.
Contraredited to several film legends who left the craft relatively soon, Newman remained in the industry for a long time, even though he denounced Hollywood with its glimpses, flamboyance and concessions.
French filmmaker Bertrand Tavernier regarded him, not without humour, "a vivid appeal of underplaying", judiciarily that in his feats he was pushing too hard.
For the beautiful Paul Newman, to whom the roles came as a platinum, the profession wasn't always so tender.
However, the first lovers played less often than outsiders: neurotics, alcoholics, lumps and losers whose decline and revolt revolt in its perfect traits.
As director Newman, he uncovered little-known aspects of his shy sensitivity.
His 1968 film Rachel, Rachel (according to Canadian Margaret Laurence's novel), starring his wife Joanne Woodward, gives a sensitive female portrait full of melancholy.
His son Scott, whom he had lost because of an overdose, was devoted in 1984 to the film Harry and Son, a work full of shame and mourning.
His great comrade and former collaborator Robert Redford (playing together in The Sting and the Butchy Cassidy and the Sundance Kid) grieled: "His presence made my life and this country better."
Magnificentness, love of life, such are the main qualities of the deceased an actor.
Commitment to his legendary career, the great civil rights activist, the eco-ecriterry, the independent film, an opponent of Hollywood's decay, is also leaving.
We were accustomed accustomed to seeing vintage vintage vintage, sauces, biscuits and other groceries, which may have seemed quite tasteless to us, although at first it was a gag.
However, the profits from the sale went to the account of his Foundation for a Difficult Childhood.
Newman thus, rather than being lulled with fame, engaged in society until the very last moment.
His five daughters left a letter containing these sentences: "Always and to the end, your father was grateful to his happy planet.
“It was an honor that I could have been here.”
And for us it was an honor to be able to follow the life path of such a lucrative and genetuous American artist.
And besides, after all, a exemplary citizen.
What was being produced at the Zuschlag & Co. invoice factory?
Before long, on October 8, the trial will begin in criminal proceedings against János Zuschlag and his associates.
In addition to other felonies, the Politician and his associates have been charged with long-established and systematically criminal organizations, including forgery of deceivers, as a result of which exceptionally significant damages have been caused.
According to Prosecutor's Office, they used the money raised in public tenders for their own purposes and often documented the fulfillment of the tasks with fictitious invoices.
Mories from the state and self-government - a total of approximately 65 million forints - traveled partly to Fiatal Baldall's treason, partly into the pockets of individuals.
The manner already reported by the investigating authority consisted in the fact that the money obtained in public tenders was levied on the basis of invoicing for which there was no real consideration, and the commitments received by the associations never fulfilled.
According to the indictment, a large proportion of invoices were false.
Subscriptions for these invoices came from Józsefváros market, round stamps were produced in Kiskunhalasi.
It was decided, among other things, about the names of which companies the production of invoices should take place, among other things, on a tour along the northern bank of the Balaton, to which István Lados János Zuschlag.
Depending on his testimonies, the former was supposed to look for guesthouses and restaurants.
In them he asked for bills for his consumption, according to whose model the invoices submitted within the framework of public competitions announced, inter alia, by the Ministry of Youth and Sport, the Ministry of Labour and Social Affairs or the Self-government of the capital, were then produced.
Invoice was exhibited mostly by István Lados with his companion András Őrim, who, according to our information, most often wrote reports needed to obtain subsidies.
In his "study journey" Lados chose a beer hall.
Pursuant to two invoices Issued by Zusschlage and its associates in 2003, this hospitary catering facility was ensured for a nineti-member group from BIztos Pont.
However, so many people, according to the company's leader, would not suddenly fit into this facility.
Likewise swarmed with formal and content errors an invoid issued in the summer of 2002 by a foundation called Jobb Jövőért, later Együtt and Harmadik Évezredért.
The guest house in Badacsonytomaya had only three rooms, more than ten people couldn't sleep in it one evening, yet one hundred and thirty guests were listed on the invoice.
Compulserators of forms with a rich fantasy override it even when they put on the documents a company dedicated to the hospitality industry - Pigal s. r. o., in whose accounts, according to the information provided to the Public Prosecutor's Office, documents sounding the name Jobb Jövőért and Hoppá didn't even figure.
The company's manager Győző Farkas told hvg.hu that when he was summoned to Prosecutors and showed him invoices, he immediately knew they were false documents.
"The name of our business and our tax number were in the wrong place."
As he added, in addition to the formalities, the fact that according to the invoice they accommodated a hundred people, because they have only eleven rooms that do not have such a large capacity.
In addition, catering has also been listed on the invoice, while their restaurant has not been functioning for a long time.
Outrageous producers of invoices did not conclute the fact that the Budapest travel agency is organizing only foreign trips and on an invoice with payment in cash, which also did not coinciate with the invoicing practice of the company, they foolishly cited as a mediation of a travel service around Hungary.
In addition, as it emerged during the course of the investigation, they also stated VAT in the document, although organizing trips to countries outside the European Union has been freed from VAT.
On the four documents exhibited by Jobb Jövőért by Hotel Révfülöp s. r. o., among other things, the amount of VAT disagreed, among other things. The activities of the company are not covered by a 25 percent but 15 per cent VAT, in addition, the employees of the hotel exhibited only printed invoices, but the invoice produced was hand-painted.
In addition, the "payers" spoiled the invoice, for example, by stating at one company how it emerged thanks to the investigation of the Public Prosecutor's Office, as an executable activity of road transport of goods, which the company, originally based on investment advice, did not carry out.
The fact that the invoices issued by Együtt and Harmadik Évezredért and the associations XXI. Szadi Kulturáłis Egyesület and Biztos Pont have also flowed out because of formal deviations - inconspicuous the format of the invoice and the false stamp.
As in the case of Ravenna k. s. or the sports camp in Kunfehértó, whose representatives have denied that they had issued invoices.
Counterfegliers, for example, did not even notice the fact that HIB s. r. o. from Nyíregyházy was at the time (2001), when a group from Fiatal Városért was catering, in liquidation, which is why, according to our information, the liquidation commissioner of the company also denied that he had issued the paper.
Invoices exhibited consciously
The second group of invoicers consists of those who knew to issue a fictitious invoice.
The Esély Budapestért Foundation issued bills of about four million forints for Harmadik Évezredért at the request of Fiatal Balldal - Ifjú Szocialist.
According to an indictment, Collabb s. r. o. the head of Collabba was incapacitated to issue a fictitious account by Ludovic Györfi.
Biogate s. r. o, currently in liquidity, which in 2003 stockpiled Jobb Jövőért and Atlasz and Vörösfenyőyőyő, with invoices worth approximately five million forints, during which there was no actual economic activity, was also cooperated with Zuschlage and his associates.
Even the movement of the money, because the created invoices were later canceled, which, of course, the organizations forgot to indicate in their documents.
Another group of invoicing companies includes those that had ties to the defendants.
Thus, for example, Iván Kubatov was an authorized representative of the Ukrainian managing director Delta Trió s. r. o., engaged in the trading of fuel and motorized vehicles, headquartered in Budapez, on which, however, the company cannot be found.
In October, November and December 2005, the company issued several invoicment for the sale of computing funds worth approximately 18 million forints.
According to the data obtained by the investigation, these invoices were purchased by the Kiskunhalas company Cash Investment s. r. o., which had been liquidated since September 14, 2005.
The managing director of this company was a man from Romania, to whom Iván Kubatov was also supposed to hand over detenuencies related to the company from 2002-2005.
As we know, Kubatov acknowledged during an investigation that on behalf of the company he issued invoices to Atlasz, Hoppá and the Együttle and Harmadik Évezredért Foundation and himself accepted their contradiction.
Speaking at the request of Ivan Kubatov, Romanian bricklayers were founded Fa-Bani Jos Faipari s. r. o. and Jos-Investment k.
In fact, however, not one of the companies worked, according to the defendant because they did not get a job.
Nevertheless, the companies benefited him, because at the request of the co-defeated advocator Zsolt Szente, who also prepared their founding deeds on behalf of the companies, he issued invoices on behalf of the companies to the associations Atlasz and Y-Generáció connected to Zuschlago.
On Behalf of Investment, Delta Trió, Fa-Bani Jos, Jos Investment and Linaxtrade Kubatov gave organizations a total of 15 invoices worth 14.2 million forints.
Prosecutor's Prosecutor's Office concluded that Kubatov received 10 per cent of the amounts listed on invoices and VAT.
To issue fictitious invoices, this time for a selection procedure for Biztos Pont, the man also used the company Szi-Beri k.
In January 2006, Y-Generáció and Szövetség and Modern Magyarországért filed proposals for the Milhály Táncsices (TMA) Public Beneficial Organization of the Socialist Party (TMA), a publicly beneficial organization of the Socialist Party.
They received after 500 thousand forints, but did not execulate the amounts to the objectives set out in the proposals.
In order not to turn it out, TMA submitted five fictitious invoices from Works Team s. r. o.
After all, these invoices were found during a house search at Árpáda Kemecsei's office at the Ministry of Education.
During the trial, some of the defendants are likely to describe the course of the production of invoices, as they have already done at the Prosecutor's Office.
It may be rather interesting if he decides to reveal everything by the main defendant János Zuschlag himself.
His testimony so far is not very detailed, and although he has repeatedly vowed to unsettle everything, he has not yet done so.
The question is whether it is in his interest - in exchanging a large part of the damage, fifty million forints, perhaps the socialists have made a deal with him, and Zusi will take it.
After all, he may have been offended so far, because his requests to alleviate the detaining conditions of his deceased, i.e. placing under house arrest, have remained unanswered.
While perpetrators of economic crimes, which have done much greater damage, which have not yet been compensated, are free to walk through or at least wait for an end against the proceedings conducted in their homes, he does not have this option.
Psychology trumping: why don't we spend more money?
At auctions, customers are willing to spend more money, overestimate goods.
The neurological and economic foundations of this well-familiatory - seemingly irrational behavior have managed to be uncovered by researchers in the field of neurology and insurgency at the University of New York.
According to their study, published in the journal Science, people don’t want to lag behind in an eBay Auction competition, so they’d rather pay too high a price.
Through an experimental auction, the research was attempting to map the scheme of this "game" in the nervous system.
One group of volunteers planted, the other the group participated in a live-action Auction, using the Functional Magnetic Resonance Resonance (fMRI method) to investigate the active areas of the brain of experimental subjects.
In both games, participants were able to win the money, but when playing an auction, an important element of which is to trumpet the other side, began to intensively function when losing, a unit located under the cerebral crust, called striatum.
In addition to many other functions, this cerebral region plays a role in the "self-remutilation" mechanism of the nervous system.
According to the researchers, unsmearing the price can therefore be interpreted by trying to escalate a sharp reaction of striata.
In order to profess their theory, the members of the research team of economists carried out a financial cross-curricular investigation.
Under different conditions, three groups objected to one partner.
The control group was simply communicated, what is the fair value of the product, and they made bets.
In addition, the members of the next group were promised that if they come out of the game victorious, they would receive $15 as a reward.
On the contrary, the third group received $15 already before the auction, but in the event of a loss, its members also lost this money.
Therefore, the difference between the two groups consisted in the fact that one was emphasized the win and the second loss was emphasized.
However, the members of the group pretending "against the loss" were willing to go higher than was in the control and "victory" group, confirming the hypothesis of neurologists.
"These results cannot be deminuded from any pre-existing economic theory.
Until now, they have been explaining phenomena observable during auctions with the joy of victory and avoiding risk.
It wasn’t until the neurological Immaging methods helped us solve the discrepancy between these two theories so that we have now come to a third explanation,” said Andrew Schotter, a professor at the Faculty of Economics at the University of New York.
Hepatitis: when to consult a doctor?
Approximately half a billion people around the world suffer from a chronic hepatitis B or C infection, in Hungary this chronic liver disease is listed among the main causes of death.
The number of domestic cases of hepatitis infection is estimated at one hundred thousand, but only seven thousand of them are being cured. The reason for this is that patients often do not know that they are infected.
The name hepatitis is the collective name of infectious liver damage caused by various viruses.
There are many resembencies in their symptoms, symptomatic is inflammation of the liver and jaundice, but the causative agents of the disease are different from each other.
Hepatitis, depending on the causative agents of the disease, spread in two main ways: hepatitis A and E through the digestive system (e.g. infected foods, water), hepatitis of type B, C, D and other blood viruses and body fluids (sperma, vaginal secretion, saliva).
In any case, travellers should be protected by vaccinations against virus A and B, there is no vaccine against the type C virus.
Hepatitis A symptoms appear two to three weeks after ingestion of infected food, they are usually accompanied by nausea, weakness, abdominal problems, compulsion to vomit.
After that, jaundice develops jaundice on the scalp and eyeblindrical stool and darkens urine. The treatment can last up to two to three weeks.
Every year, a million people around the world die from a more serious kind of the disease, liver cancer and liver cirrhosis caused by hepatitis.
The main cause is that, according to estimates, only one in ten infected person is medically treated.
Hepatitis C can also have very serious consequences: if left untreated, it can lead up to hepatic cirrhosis or liver cancer.
Most of those infected do not even know about their disease, the causative agent of the disease destroys the liver cells insidiously, and so the first symptoms occur in many cases only in 20-30 years.
That's why it is very important timely prevention, the implementation of regular depreciation.
In three groups, this disease occurs a lot more often than on average: among people who underwent blood transfusions before 1991, among drug users and among people with a tattoo.
At the same time, the projected worldwide number of individuals infected with chronic hepatitis C virus is 200 million.
Since the disease can prove already a routine laboratory examination, a person should contact his/her general practitioner if he notices any symptom of an unfamiliar difficher.
With early detection, the disease is curable, the virus can be eliminated from the organism, thus preventing contagiousness and preventing the development of cancer.
On September 30, hepatitis is a world-class day, organized for the first time worldwide in 2004.
Its purpose is to draw attention to the chronic inflammation of the liver caused by these viruses, the causes of its formation and the importance of early detection of the disease.
Those who believe in God doesn’t hurt so much?
According to the results of the recent research, faith in God works as a certain analgesic, which may have relieved the death of Catholic martyrs.
Scientists at Oxford University conducted an intriguing experiment, researching how a person's belief in the god's perception of pain, the British newspaper Telegraph reported.
As part of a rather bizarre rediscussion, they underwent 12 Catholic believers and the same number of atheists with electric shocks while they all observed a painting depicting the Virgin Mary.
According to the results, Catholic believers were able to expel a large part of the pain.
Thanks to technology inquising the human brain inquising, it also turned out that Catholics have been able to activate the part of their brain responsible for regulating pain.
The research is the first of a series of research, in addition to academies involving scientists, philosophers and theologians from different parts of the university.
Exactly the test proceeded in such a way that they attached a sparking tool to the left hand of the experimental subject, which emitted electric shocks.
Researchers have asked the participants of an attempt to observe two paintings intently: Sassoferrat's Virgin Mary from the 17th-centicured 17th-centithed Republic and the Deception of Leonardo da Vinci, painted in the 15th century.
The authors of the research had hoped that the sight of the Virgin Mary would provoke a state of piety among the believers, while da Vinci's image was chosen because it does not differ too much from the former and makes a reassuring impression.
Attempting subjects spent half an hour in an MRI scanner and during this time they received 20 electroshocks in four consecutive parts, while they separately watched the image with a religious or general theme.
At the sight of the Virgin Mary they felt “safe” as if they were “took away” and “reassured themselves, they fulfilled peace.”
While watching a religious-thume painting, they felt 12 per cent less in pain than when they had Leonardo’s work in front of them.
Psychologist Miguel Farias, who also took part in the research, believes that a similar effect can be achieved with the help of any highly immersive image even among atheists, just need to find the correct photograph.
"We would have to find an image that they will perceive very positively, from the position of a mother or a father," the psychologist said.
Episcognant Bishop Tom Wright welcomed the research.
"Practification of the faith should change and in many cases also change our personality," Wright added.
After such great results, it is only a question of what effect it would have on regulating the pain of believers if they showed them a Madonna from Leonard or a painter of similar caliber.
Would the sight of a high-faictorious Virgin Mary mean achieving even better results?
You're what you're going to share from yourself
