In its conviction, the Eu Scientific Committee states that users of portable musical instruments, when using loud music (more than 89 decibels) for just five hours a week, will exceed the currently valid limits corresponding to the maximum permitted noise in the workplace.
Those who obscure music in such conditions for an extended period of time risk a permanent hearing loss after five years.
