Overcome the laws of gravity thanks to super adhesive and in the future to walk on the walls like Spider-Man.
This is the object of various U.S. research centers, and now a team of four institutes came very close.
Scientists managed to keep a hundred-kilogram body glued on a vertical wall using a sticker of just 2.5 square centimeters.
STUDIUM – The U.S. journal Science publishes the discoveries of some researchers at Dayton in Dayton, in Acron, the Georgia Institute of Technology and the Air Force Research Laboratory.
The material invented by a team of researchers is the development of already-existing materials, which use a special carbon dwarf cruciate structure.
“We can conceubmit the basis of the glue as a series of pipes laid as an arranged pile of spaghetti» explains Zhong Lin Wang from the Georgia Institute of Technology in Atlanta.
The scientists were inspired by gecko's legs, covered with microscopic hairs, which allow the animal to ensure a perfect adhesions.
Executions carried out on a variety of materials such as glass, Teflon and glazing paper have shown that the new adhesive is ten times stronger than the feet of these reptiles, and at the same time it is simply peels away from the wall» explains Liming Dai, a researcher of the Engineering Faculty of Dayton University.
COMFOVABLOBIT BREAMS? -"This material could be useful as a makeshift adhesive» supplied by Liming Dai.
Perhaps to walk on walls like Spider-man? Perhaps yes, but researchers are thinking about a far less fascinating use as a combination of electrical devices, because dwarf carbon pipes are conductors of heat and electrical energy.
Additional applications could involve aeronautical space engineering.
For the time being, there aren't superheroes.
FRESH RESPONDENT – The University of Berkley in California is also dedicated to researching a new adhesive.
In an American Chemical Society magazine, California researchers introduced micro-fibre-formed adhesifed adhesive as a hair that cleanses itself from the dust by movement on an area to maintain perfect snugness.
Medications: Never with Juice
Attention to grapefruit, orange and apple juice.
If you take these drinks, which are consumed mainly in the summer, because they are refreshing and full of vitamins, along with certain life-saving drugs, their ingestion changes intensification or a decrease in effectiveness with serious health consequences.
For David Bailey, a professor of Western Ontario University in London to emphasize the risks of juices both ready-to-done and fresh in combination with the ingestion of certain medications, the just-conceived 263rd National Meeting of the American Chemical Society in Philadelphia raises a new alarm: it only takes one glass of grape, an orange and cider julence to reduce the absorption of certain life-saving drugs.
Grep juice has already bequeraded that he is responsible for raising the effects of certain anti-arithmic drugs, antibiotics, anxiolitics, antibiotics, anti-hystamines and neurological drugs.
DECISOR TO ENTREGONE – This was reported by the Italian Medical Agency itself in the newsletter two years ago and roused doctors and patients not to underestimate the dangers arising out of this mixture and to be careful about what they drank if they are taking drugs such as Diazepam or Methadone.
NOT JUST GRAPEFRUIT – According to experts, orange and apple juice also contain substances that dampen the drugs.
A lengthy list of effects submerged with grapefruit and other juices.
From there Michele Carruba's appeal, director of the pharmacological department of the State University of Milan: "Such discoveries are usually immediately announced to various international and national pharmacy agencies, which will eventually be arranged and replaced by medical information instructions.
So always read illustrative leaves of drugs that you get and if you come across something obssecure, don’t be alarmed, but ask a doctor or a pharmacist for clarification.”
Nobel under Economics Paul Krugman
The Nobel Prize was awarded to American Paul Krugman for his studies of commercial models and localization of economic activities.
Krugman is a 55-year-old Novokeňan who teaches at the University of Priceton who is a well-known New York Times editor.
Krugman is one of the most important critics when it comes to foreign, economic, and political actions of the Bush administration.
Few months after the assassinations in September 2001, the days when Enron went bust, Krugman predicted in a commentary published in the New York Times that the second event would, in the sense of the consequences on the history of the United States, much more important than the first.
Prediction, which provoked many controversies and that was reproached him for years, which, however, turned out to be accurate.
“I am amazed and was shocked at the speed with which collapsues such as Enron and Worldcom have vanished out of public interest, Krugman said at the end of 2002.
According to Lorenzo Bini Smaghi of the Executive Committee of the Central European Bank, Krugman is an "economist of great importance", but also a popularizer who has a "very aggressive style, especially critical of the excerpts of the Bush Liberalist Administration".
Open Office, here we have the third release of "anti-Microsoft »
“It’s Open Office.org 3.0, an open-source passenger-making package that’s moving towards more and more users, from home to the office, from experts to public administration, as a free alternative to the most well-familiar Microsoft Office.
After about a one-hundred-per-year work of volunteer workers inspected by SUN Microsystem, the new Open Office is shown to the general public with a variety of novelties: the welcome screen and the revised and improved opening window will be joined by other, much more substantial ones, such as the compatibility for the Apple Mac OS X corpstrual system and support for the new ODF (Open Document Format) 1.2, the last standard version of ISO.
Emphasis is also based on working with the Office 2007, Open Office is also able to open a document with a new Microsoft extension (.docx, .xlsx, .pptx).
Interesting are the special functions of some models, such as what makes it possible to reduce the dimensions of the PowerPoint presentation, useful for example for transmission by electronic means, or the ability to transfer a PDF folder to a graphic design model and maintain the original appearance of the page.
From this point of view, we can still create "PDF hybrids" documents, which are similar to typical Adobe graphics and have the properties of a spreadsheet processor or text program.
Collaboration is an element that has received many enhancements within application programs: in Excel it is possible to work together between different users and to avoid conflicts on changes, in a text program each collaborator is assigned one color to comments in order to be a clearer identification in the revision phase.
Some companies are also working to transfer some Open Office features to the Web (on the cloud), and in the next few weeks they should mislebuiorate a definite result.
The Italian version can be downloaded at http://it.openoffice.org/download/3.0.0/download300.html, it has been added to the English version, which can be found on the mirror from Friday.
In Addition to Windows and Mac OS, as usual, the package is also available for the Linux operating system.
Also, the installation cd can be sent at home or to the workplace on request.
And if the topic of gruiness can be a draw for expansion in households, it is on the Open Office’s business area the package relies a lot, and it can already take into account a variety of projects implemented in public administration and in schools.
And there are also offers of training, consultations and assistance services ideal for small and medium-sized companies, which could open business perspectives.
Open Office consists of five main models: Writer, for video typing replacing Word; Calc is a spreadsheet aimed at replacing an Excel; Immipress for Presentations Similar to Powerpoint; Dbase, as in the case of the most famous Access, is a program that allows you to work on databases; Draw, eventually, is a graphic model.
The goal for the year 2008 is to achieve 5 million downloads, and when we consider that to today we are almost 3 million and 600 thousand, with the release of the new version, it is possible that this anticipated number can be surpassed.
