In Addition to Chevron, Verdant Power Inc. From New York and Ocean Power from New Jersey are also following a trace of marine energy, and the sums invested so far, although they are not well-argued, show an increasing interest, according to observers.
The technology it needs to be developed.
Experts are talking about technology, which is still in the early days, because we do not know the impact the use of marine energy will have on the environment.
For the time being, establishments in Portugal and some in Scotland there are small dimensions, and they do not appear to be causing major ecosystem problems.
However, it is necessary to use technologies with a greater impact on the mezzanine.
The methods are different: Ocean Power, for example, it uses a combat system that are intertwined with each other.
The force of the waves, which moves with buoys up and down, is altered with the help of cylinders and cylinders to the hydraulic pressure within these buoches.
Tissues the turbine, which delivers energy to the generator.
Energie goes ashore by underwater cables.
For the time being, there are four devices of this type at the project phase, waiting only for federal approvement and part of the energy could be used for military purposes.
Verdant Power, on the other hand, it already generates energy for a shopping mall and a car park using six sub-seating turbines in New York's East River.
The movement of water during tides during tide causes turbines to rotate, which feeds the generator with this rotating movement.
Verdant stated that they have a long list of clients awaiting necessary authorizations due to the possibility of using this energy.
After the waves, after tides and after tides.
